<BaseLayout
  title="Disclaimer — Freightgcc"
  description="What Freightgcc does and does not claim: editorial analysis, not customs or legal advice; ranges and simulations, not quotations; no clearance guarantee."
>
  <article>
    <h1>Disclaimer</h1>
    <p class="article-meta">Last reviewed 15 November 2026</p>

    <p class="lede">
      Freightgcc publishes editorial analysis about moving goods from China to the six GCC markets. It
      is not a freight forwarder, carrier, customs broker, insurer or law firm, and it does not act on
      your behalf. This page states precisely what the content can and cannot be relied on for. It is
      written to be read alongside the <a href="/terms/">terms of use</a> and the
      <a href="/methodology/">methodology</a>, not instead of them.
    </p>

    <h2>1. Editorial analysis, not professional advice</h2>
    <p>
      The content is journalism and analysis. It is not legal, customs, tax, accounting, insurance,
      trade-compliance or engineering advice, and reading it does not create a professional
      relationship of any kind — including a lawyer–client, broker–client or adviser–client
      relationship.
    </p>
    <p>
      Customs classification, duty rates, certificate requirements, port rules and documentary
      requirements are decided by the competent authority for each market and can change without
      notice. A position that is correct for one consignment can be wrong for another with a different
      HS line, a different end use, a different importer of record or a different origin. Before you
      act, obtain a ruling or written confirmation from the authority, or from a licensed broker or
      adviser acting for you and carrying the professional risk.
    </p>

    <h2>2. Ranges, simulations and illustrative figures are not quotations</h2>
    <p>
      Freight rates, transit times, clearance durations and charges are published as ranges, as
      illustrative examples, or as the output of a calculator using inputs you supply. They are not
      offers, not quotations, not bookings and not a commitment by Freightgcc or by any carrier.
    </p>
    <p>
      The calculators perform arithmetic on the numbers you enter. They do not fetch live rates, do not
      know your HS classification, and do not validate your inputs against any authority. A result is
      only as good as the assumptions entered. Where a page presents a <strong>case simulation</strong>,
      the assumptions are stated in a parameter table; the arithmetic is shown so that a reader can
      check it, and the limitations of the model are listed beside the result.
    </p>

    <h2>3. No guarantee of clearance, transit or commercial outcome</h2>
    <p>
      Nothing on this site guarantees that a consignment will clear customs, that a certificate will be
      accepted, that a carrier will accept a booking, that a port will perform as described, or that a
      route will meet a deadline. Those outcomes depend on documents, valuation, inspection,
      carrier decisions and the actions of authorities that no publication controls.
    </p>
    <p>
      Where a page describes a risk — demurrage, rejection, rolled cargo, certificate mismatch — it is
      describing a known failure mode, not predicting what will happen to your shipment.
    </p>

    <h2>4. Third-party information and official sources</h2>
    <p>
      Pages cite regulators, port operators, customs authorities and other public sources so that a
      reader can verify a claim. Those sources can be amended, moved or withdrawn; a link working today
      may not work next month. Freightgcc does not control third-party pages and is not responsible for
      their content, accuracy or availability.
    </p>
    <p>
      A citation is not an endorsement, and a link to a regulator does not mean that the regulator has
      reviewed or approved this site. Where a page quotes a published tariff or rule, the authority's
      own text governs if the two differ.
    </p>

    <h2>5. Independence and funding</h2>
    <p>
      Freightgcc does not sell freight, book space, clear goods, insure cargo, or receive commissions,
      referral fees or payment from carriers, forwarders, brokers or port operators. Where a company or
      port is named, it is named because it is relevant to the analysis, not because of a commercial
      relationship. If that position ever changes, it will be disclosed on the page where the
      relationship is relevant and on the <a href="/about/">about page</a>.
    </p>

    <h2>6. Accuracy, completeness and timeliness</h2>
    <p>
      Pages carry a last-reviewed date. The site is corrected when an error is confirmed, and material
      corrections are recorded on the <a href="/corrections/">corrections page</a>. No warranty is given
      that any page is accurate, complete or current at the moment you read it, or that it covers every
      route, port, product or regulatory change relevant to your shipment.
    </p>
    <p>
      The absence of a topic is not a statement that the topic is unimportant or that no rule applies.
      It usually means the information did not meet the standard for publication. Where a page says a
      figure is unverified or unavailable, that is a deliberate statement, not an omission to be filled
      by assumption.
    </p>

    <h2>7. Forward-looking statements</h2>
    <p>
      Statements about future capacity, rates, congestion, regulation or transit times are estimates or
      expectations, not predictions. Market conditions, fuel prices, seasonal demand, Red Sea routing,
      port disruptions and regulatory decisions can change faster than any static page. Do not treat a
      forward-looking statement on this site as a commitment by any party.
    </p>

    <h2>8. External links, downloads and third-party tools</h2>
    <p>
      Links to official documents, PDFs and third-party sites are provided for verification and further
      reading. Downloads are not scanned or warranted by Freightgcc, and third-party tools are governed
      by their own terms and privacy policies. Opening a third-party link takes you outside this site.
    </p>

    <h2>9. Limitation of liability</h2>
    <p>
      To the fullest extent permitted by applicable law, Freightgcc is not liable for any loss arising
      from reliance on the content, including demurrage, storage, inspection, penalties, lost profit,
      lost contracts or business interruption. The full limitation and the governing-law clause are in
      the <a href="/terms/">terms of use</a>. Nothing in this disclaimer excludes liability that cannot
      lawfully be excluded, or affects mandatory consumer rights in your jurisdiction.
    </p>

    <h2>10. How to verify a claim before relying on it</h2>
    <ol>
      <li>Identify the claim and the date it was last reviewed.</li>
      <li>Follow the cited source and read the current version at the authority's own site.</li>
      <li>Check that the HS line, origin, importer of record and end use match your shipment.</li>
      <li>Where money is at stake, obtain written confirmation from the authority or a licensed broker.</li>
      <li>If the page and the authority disagree, the authority governs — and please
        <a href="/contact/">tell us</a> so the page can be corrected.</li>
    </ol>

    <h2>11. Reporting an error</h2>
    <p>
      If a claim on this site is wrong, report it through the <a href="/contact/">contact page</a> with
      the page URL, the sentence and, where possible, the source that shows the error. The process and
      response standards are set out on <a href="/corrections/">corrections</a>.
    </p>

